      "headline": {
        "en": "Moody's: US life insurers increasingly use rated note feeders for private credit",
        "zh": "穆迪：美国人寿保险公司日益依赖RNF"
      },
      "summary": {
        "en": "US life insurers are increasingly using rated note feeders (RNFs) to access private credit markets, according to Moody's Ratings. Moody's estimates that 35 per cent of US life insurance investments go towards private credit, and notes RNFs carry credit and operational risks amplified by limited transparency. The National Association of Insurance Commissioners has expanded scrutiny of insurers' private credit investments, with regulatory review of RNFs ongoing.",
        "zh": "穆迪评级表示，美国人寿保险公司正日益使用评级票据载体（RNF）来获取私募信贷市场的敞口。穆迪估计，美国人寿保险投资的35%投向私募信贷，并指出RNF存在信用和运营风险，且因透明度有限而放大。美国保险监督官协会已扩大对保险公司私募信贷投资的审查，对RNF的监管审查仍在进行中。"
      },
